        <mxCell id="c52" value="&lt;i&gt;The three results of the Expected results: the test of Tests.dax for fiscal 2026, before the change, after Revenue sums ListAmount in place of LineTotal, and after the restore. The test reads the measure. Other queries or visuals using [Revenue] also change; these column-based cards do not. Highlighted: the test after the change. Below: what a saved version keeps, what it leaves out, and what a project under version control adds. The window of Save to version history and the restore control were not read in the author&#x27;s test, so the figure draws their effect, not their windows.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="524" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
